    ' aria-labelledby="prompt-title">\n' +
      '        <div class="section-header"><span class="section-index">04</span><div><h2 id="prompt-title">AI Prompt</h2><p class="section-kicker">Review the boundary. Plan the build. Verify the actual runtime.</p></div></div>\n' +
      '        <p class="architecture-note">Reusable showcase prompts — not historical submissions. Each step is a public development guide for this type of application.</p>\n' +
      '        <div class="pulse-prompt-steps">\n' +
      '          <details class="pulse-details"><summary>01 · Review</summary><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-toolbar"><span class="code-label">Review the source</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="pulseReviewPrompt">Copy Review</button></div><pre tabindex="0"><code id="pulseReviewPrompt">Review the supplied React application and container files.\n' +
      'Identify browser components, API handlers, runtime state,\n' +
      'build dependencies, exposed ports, and existing Compose projects.\n' +
      'Separate decorative examples from measured runtime values.\n' +
      'List protected files and possible port or network collisions.\n' +
      'Do not change existing applications.</code></pre></div></details>\n' +
      '          <details class="pulse-details"><summary>02 · Plan</summary><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-toolbar"><span class="code-label">Plan one isolated application</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="pulsePlanPrompt">Copy Plan</button></div><pre tabindex="0"><code id="pulsePlanPrompt">Plan a small React runtime dashboard with responsive notifications.\n' +
      'Use one Node application image and multiple equivalent replicas.\n' +
      'Define a pinned multi-stage build, non-root execution, health checks,\n' +
      'CPU/memory budgets, restart policy, and non-secret environment settings.\n' +
      'Use a dedicated Compose project, network, image tag, and loopback port.\n' +
      'Keep scaling in a trusted terminal, not in the public browser.\n' +
      'Map each requirement to an actual verification step.</code></pre></div></details>\n' +
      '          <details class="pulse-details" open><summary>03 · Build</summary><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-toolbar"><span class="code-label">Implementation specification</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="pulseBuildPrompt">Copy Build</button></div><pre tabindex="0"><code id="pulseBuildPrompt">Build Container Pulse as a small standalone App Engineering Showcase.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '1. Adapt the asymmetric CSS dashboard and container-relative cards\n' +
      '   into React components. Preserve original showcases and shared themes.\n' +
      '2. Implement a landing page, /healthz, and /api/runtime with hostname,\n' +
      '   process uptime, runtime version, and application version.\n' +
      '3. Validate real responses before updating metadata, counters, or cards.\n' +
      '   Label observations as current-page data; do not fabricate live values.\n' +
      '4. Support Check runtime, a bounded sample batch, Clear, and acknowledgment.\n' +
      '   Cancel stale work; keep acknowledgments in browser memory only.\n' +
      '5. Copy dependency manifests before installing locked dependencies.\n' +
      '   Compile in a build stage; ship only runtime assets and the server.\n' +
      '6. Run as non-root with resource limits, health checks, restart policies,\n' +
      '   and a non-secret .env file. Keep replicas interchangeable and scalable.\n' +
      '7. Use independent Compose resources and an unused localhost port.\n' +
      '   Do not restart Docker, alter older projects, or mount its socket.\n' +
      '8. Test endpoints, failures, cancellation, themes, keyboard access,\n' +
      '   actual container configuration, and two-to-three-to-two scaling.\n' +
      '   Keep source tests, real runtime evidence, and pending work distinct.</code></pre></div></details>\n' +
      '          <details class="pulse-details"><summary>04 · Verify</summary><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-toolbar"><span class="code-label">Check reality, not configuration alone</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="pulseVerifyPrompt">Copy Verify</button></div><pre tabindex="0"><code id="pulseVerifyPrompt">Run source tests, build the real image, and inspect its final contents.\n' +
      'Verify non-root identity, applied CPU/memory limits, restart policy,\n' +
      'health state, exposed ports, and environment behavior.\n' +
      'Scale two replicas to three and back; verify actual container readiness\n' +
      'and new responses after discovery updates. Restore two healthy replicas.\n' +
      'Check dashboard updates, notification acknowledgment, cancellation,\n' +
      'malformed responses, offline recovery, keyboard controls, and themes.\n' +
      'Compare prior projects before and after without modifying them.\n' +
      'Report failures and blocked checks. Never invent successful evidence.</code></pre></div></details>\n' +
      '        </div>\n' +
      '      </section>\n' +
      '      '
    
