    Use one Node application image and multiple equivalent replicas.
    Define a pinned multi-stage build, non-root execution, health checks,
    CPU/memory budgets, restart policy, and non-secret environment settings.
    Use a dedicated Compose project, network, image tag, and loopback port.
    Keep scaling in a trusted terminal, not in the public browser.
    Map each requirement to an actual verification step.</code></pre></div></details>
              <details class="pulse-details" open><summary>03 · Build</summary><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-toolbar"><span class="code-label">Implementation specification</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="pulseBuildPrompt">Copy Build</button></div><pre tabindex="0"><code id="pulseBuildPrompt">Build Container Pulse as a small standalone App Engineering Showcase.
    
    1. Adapt the asymmetric CSS dashboard and container-relative cards
       into React components. Preserve original showcases and shared themes.
    2. Implement a landing page, /healthz, and /api/runtime with hostname,
       process uptime, runtime version, and application version.
    3. Validate real responses before updating metadata, counters, or cards.
