    4. Support Check runtime, a bounded sample batch, Clear, and acknowledgment.
       Cancel stale work; keep acknowledgments in browser memory only.
    5. Copy dependency manifests before installing locked dependencies.
       Compile in a build stage; ship only runtime assets and the server.
    6. Run as non-root with resource limits, health checks, restart policies,
       and a non-secret .env file. Keep replicas interchangeable and scalable.
    7. Use independent Compose resources and an unused localhost port.
       Do not restart Docker, alter older projects, or mount its socket.
    8. Test endpoints, failures, cancellation, themes, keyboard access,
       actual container configuration, and two-to-three-to-two scaling.
       Keep source tests, real runtime evidence, and pending work distinct.</code></pre></div></details>
              <details class="pulse-details"><summary>04 · Verify</summary><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-toolbar"><span class="code-label">Check reality, not configuration alone</span><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy-target="pulseVerifyPrompt">Copy Verify</button></div><pre tabindex="0"><code id="pulseVerifyPrompt">Run source tests, build the real image, and inspect its final contents.
